{
  "id": "reading_cortices",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "description": "SOCIETY OF CORTICES \u2014 the reading as FIVE concurrent graph-resident cortices driven by the agent's cognitive_tick, NOT a linear u_dispatch chain pumped by hand-called run_rules/fire_reflexes. Each Cortex node bundles a set of AnalysisStages (its faculties) + a per-cortex Reflex that fires EVERY tick, advancing whichever of ITS stages the la_dispatch_* rules have dispatched (i.e. whose graph data-preconditions now hold). The five reflexes REPLACE the single analysis_advance reflex: all five are evaluated every tick, each processes whatever of its own inputs are ready, and the reading EMERGES from their mutual constraint over ticks. Data-dependencies still order the emergence (language must produce predications before situation can build the model) via the la_dispatch preconditions, but no cortex WAITS on a hardcoded Python stage chain -- each fires the moment its inputs exist. Stage->cortex membership is a `cortex` attr + an in_cortex edge stamped per-drive by reading_drive (mechanical); the reflex responses (<name>_cortex_advance) are thin non-branching shim lookups (_advance_cortex_stage, the _question_pursue_advance precedent).",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "reading_cortices",
    "description": "Five concurrent cortices (language/situation/social/narrative/executive), each a Cortex node + a per-tick Reflex; the reading settles as their reflexes fire over cognitive_ticks."
  },
